// split and replace scanned every position and computed the piece before each
// match as slice(last, i - last). With an overlapping separator the second match
// arrives before last, so the length went negative and String.slice panicked:
// String.split("aaaa", "aa") was a runtime error. Matches are non-overlapping
// now, which is the answer the loop was reaching for.
println(String.split("aaaa", "aa"))
println(String.replace("aaa", "aa", "b"))
println(String.replace("aaaa", "aa", "-"))
